# Planning workspace

This directory holds the rationale and evidence needed to build, use, and resume
the current version. Decisions live in `governance/decisions.yaml`. Keep this
directory concise; do not commit working drafts or raw review output.

## Rules

- Work only in the phase recorded in `governance/project-state.yaml`.
- Record decisions in `governance/decisions.yaml`; do not hide decisions in prose alone.
- Before custom implementation, document maintained open-source candidates and why each was
  adopted, adapted, deferred, or rejected.
- Define external contracts before selecting a framework implementation.
- Preserve assumptions, alternatives, evidence, known risks, and unresolved questions.
- Build in small increments after the project author explicitly approves Build.
- Ask about blockers; record nonblocking ideas once in `later.md` and keep going.

## Planned artifacts

`definition.md` and `later.md` are seeded. Create the rest only as the project reaches the
relevant stage:

- `definition.md` — seeded. The problem, how it is solved today, the value, who it is for; the
  purpose derived from them; the smallest version that delivers the value; what is not in
  the first version; success signals. Approved before Plan.
- `later.md` — seeded. Where suggestions and questions go instead of into scope.
- `solution-evaluation.md` — seeded; the evidence-backed build-or-adopt decision required
  before Build. It also records any user-provided codebase that was checked.
- `governance/project-state.yaml` — records this project's next deliverable version and its
  usable goal separately from the Agent Builder template version.
- `architecture.md` — only when the version needs explicit boundaries or contracts.
- `implementation-plan.md` — the smallest ordered build and verification plan.

Summarize consequential Review findings in an existing durable record. Keep previews,
transcripts, reviewer packets, and drafts outside the committed repository unless they
are themselves a needed product artifact.
